        <section id="material" class="inst-method-card"><span class="inst-step">04</span><h2>Material corrections</h2><p>A material correction is one that can change a reader's understanding or decision—for example a wrong price, provider, benchmark result, lifecycle status or factual conclusion. The preferred fix is to update the authoritative stored field or content record so related pages inherit the correction consistently.</p></section>
        <section id="disputes" class="inst-method-card"><span class="inst-step">05</span><h2>Disagreements & interpretation</h2><p>Not every disagreement is a factual error. Editorial judgment, benchmark interpretation and community opinion can reasonably differ. When the dispute concerns interpretation, AI Orbit should preserve the underlying evidence and clarify the basis of the conclusion rather than rewriting a measured result to match an opinion.</p></section>
        <section id="privacy" class="inst-method-card inst-warning"><span class="inst-step">06</span><h2>Submission privacy</h2><p>Do not send passwords, API keys or other sensitive credentials. Contact and correction submissions are handled under the Privacy Policy and may be retained for moderation, clarification and abuse prevention.</p><div class="inst-actions"><a class="inst-btn" href="{{ route('privacy') }}">Privacy Policy</a><a class="inst-btn" href="{{ route('sourcing-verification') }}">Sourcing & Verification</a></div></section>
